WEBVTT

NOTE EVAL FILE: made-up example. Every name, company and street is fictional.

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:11.231
Kendall Testagent: Hi, both of you. Before we start, I'm recording this Zoom so I can send you a recap afterward. Is that okay with you?

2
00:00:11.931 --> 00:00:13.531
Ellis Fakewell: Yes, that's fine.

3
00:00:14.231 --> 00:00:15.831
Jordan Fakewell's iPad: Yep.

4
00:00:16.531 --> 00:00:20.762
Kendall Testagent: Great. So you're coming from Spokane. Tell me about the move.

5
00:00:21.462 --> 00:00:30.308
Ellis Fakewell: My company is moving me to the Salt Lake office. I start January 4th. Our house here is under contract, closing December 18th.

6
00:00:31.008 --> 00:00:37.546
Kendall Testagent: Congrats on getting it under contract. So where are you between December 18th and when you buy?

7
00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:47.862
Jordan Fakewell's iPad: We've got a short-term rental in Draper for January and February. So we'd like to close by the end of February, March at the latest.

8
00:00:48.562 --> 00:00:50.869
Kendall Testagent: Okay. What are you looking for?

9
00:00:51.569 --> 00:01:01.569
Ellis Fakewell: Single family, three bedrooms at least, and we have a camper, so RV parking is a must. Like a gate and a side pad, 40 feet.

10
00:01:02.269 --> 00:01:06.115
Jordan Fakewell's iPad: And a shop or a three-car garage. Ellis builds furniture.

11
00:01:06.815 --> 00:01:14.123
Kendall Testagent: RV parking with at least 40 feet on the side, and a shop or a three-car garage. Lot size?

12
00:01:14.823 --> 00:01:18.669
Ellis Fakewell: A quarter acre or more, probably, to fit all that.

13
00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:20.969
Kendall Testagent: Areas?

14
00:01:21.669 --> 00:01:26.285
Jordan Fakewell's iPad: Draper, Riverton, Herriman. Ellis will be downtown, so within 35, 40 minutes.

15
00:01:26.985 --> 00:01:44.677
Ellis Fakewell: About that. We drove through a few places when we visited in September. I'll be honest, Cobble Ridge in Riverton was a lot of big families, kids everywhere, and you heard a lot of Spanish at the park. We'd want somewhere a little more like us.

16
00:01:45.377 --> 00:02:07.685
Kendall Testagent: I hear you. I can't help you choose a neighborhood based on who lives there. That's fair housing, and it applies to me no matter what. What I can do is show you the things that actually separate these areas: lot sizes, HOA rules on RVs, commute times. And you're welcome to visit anywhere and decide for yourselves.

17
00:02:08.385 --> 00:02:09.985
Ellis Fakewell: Sure, that's fair.

18
00:02:10.685 --> 00:02:17.223
Jordan Fakewell's iPad: HOA rules on RVs is a big one, actually. Our HOA here made people move their trailers.

19
00:02:17.923 --> 00:02:30.231
Kendall Testagent: That's a hard filter, then. I'll only send homes with no HOA or an HOA that allows RV parking on the lot, and we'll read the CC&Rs on anything you're serious about.

20
00:02:30.931 --> 00:02:35.546
Jordan Fakewell's iPad: And how are the schools in Lakeview Heights? A coworker mentioned it.

21
00:02:36.246 --> 00:02:47.400
Kendall Testagent: For schools, I'll point you to the sources: the district's boundary lookup and the state's school report card. I'll send both links so you can see the data yourselves.

22
00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.700
Jordan Fakewell's iPad: Okay, perfect.

23
00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.000
Kendall Testagent: Price range?

24
00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:56.546
Ellis Fakewell: Up to 750. We'd love to be closer to 700.

25
00:02:57.246 --> 00:02:58.846
Kendall Testagent: And a lender?

26
00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:07.623
Ellis Fakewell: We're preapproved with Sample Pacific Lending. It's a conventional loan, and the letter's from October. Our loan officer is Rory Fakename.

27
00:03:08.323 --> 00:03:12.938
